  "results": [
    "All three inputs and outputs retain selected HEADER values DIMASZ=.18, DIMEXO=.0625, DIMTXT=.18 and DIMTIH=1. Input and output DXFs pass ezdxf audits.",
    "For the omitted and explicit-header cases, ODA-generated DWG frames encode those four legacy values; ODA reopen omits all four corresponding groups. ezdxf 1.4.5 returns 2.5, .625, 2.5 and 0 as its effective defaults for omitted groups.",
    "For the distinct case, input DXF, DWG physical frame and reopened DXF all explicitly retain DIMASZ=7.25, DIMEXO=3.5, DIMTXT=9.25 and DIMTIH=0. These are distinguishable from the unchanged HEADER values.",
    "The shared ODA-spec frame observer verifies physical fields and handle roles in each generated DWG, rejects every byte-prefix truncation and four wrong-role mutations, and retries successfully. Original pair results are byte-for-byte unchanged.",
    "The comparison helper now separately reports explicit and omitted groups and reader-effective defaults; its omitted and explicit-mismatch controls pass. Three related AC1012 handle-role CTests pass.",
    "This corrects the interpretation of earlier DIMSTYLE divergence receipts: their reported DXF numbers were ezdxf effective defaults for absent groups, not explicit values present in the files.",
    "The original witness pair was repackaged without regenerating drawings; its handoff now states the omission and reader-default limitation accurately."
  ],
